{"toolCallId":"call_edfe38366d314f9b8a762fb5608943d3","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/spec.md:93:| REQ-007 | With `--quiet`, any warning `recommend-level.sh` writes to stderr is still written to stderr, unchanged and in full. `--quiet` trims stdout only: it never suppresses, redirects or reformats a warning bound for stderr. |\nspecs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md:51:- [ ] T018 Implement REQ-007: `output_quiet()` writes the level line to stdout and returns, and no `>&2` warning site is gated on `QUIET_OUTPUT`, so `--quiet` trims stdout only (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`)\nspecs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/acceptance-criteria.md:62:| AC-009 | REQ-007 | Given an invocation in which `recommend-level.sh` writes a warning to stderr, When the same invocation runs with `--quiet`, Then the warning still appears on stderr in full and only stdout is trimmed | Capture stdout and stderr to separate files with and without `--quiet` on the same stderr-producing input; assert the stderr files are identical and the `--quiet` stdout is one line | Unmet | - |\n--- files ---\ntotal 144\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 10 michelkerkmeester  wheel    320 26 Oct 15:04 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 michelkerkmeester  wheel     96 26 Oct 14:58 ..\n-rw-------@  1 michelkerkmeester  wheel   5593 26 Oct 15:03 acceptance-criteria.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  wheel    423 26 Oct 14:58 description.json\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  wheel   5916 26 Oct 15:04 graph-metadata.json\n-rw-------@  1 michelkerkmeester  wheel   2474 26 Oct 15:02 implementation-summary.md\n-rw-------@  1 michelkerkmeester  wheel  17788 26 Oct 15:01 plan.md\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 michelkerkmeester  wheel     96 26 Oct 14:58 scratch\n-rw-------@  1 michelkerkmeester  wheel  13152 26 Oct 15:03 spec.md\n-rw-------@  1 michelkerkmeester  wheel  10087 26 Oct